            <ArticleTitle>Modification of pain on injection of propofol. A comparison of pethidine and lignocaine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One hundred and fifty ASA 1 and 2 patients were randomly allocated to receive pethidine 25 mg (1 ml), lignocaine 10 mg (1 ml) or 0.9% saline (1 ml) on a double-blind basis, as pretreatment to reduce pain on injection of propofol. Both active treatments were significantly better than placebo at preventing pain (p &lt; 0.01). Lignocaine was most effective in preventing pain in men (p &lt; 0.05) whilst pethidine was more effective in women (p &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
